{"run": "0081", "session": "0006-horizon-review-ajc", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1041", "title": "A DIRECTORY-LEVEL 'git add' ON THE SHARED INDEX CAN STAGE ANOTHER LANE'S FILE FOR DELETION -- the file is present at HEAD and present on disk, and the index still says D. The next lane to commit anything destroys it, and the commit is theirs, not yours.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:39:26.656680+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1038", "title": "AJC's hgraph HAS the same stale-node class as AJCR (I-1004) but it does NOT reach the frontier -- so it is documentation rot, not misdirected work. Do not copy AJCR's remediation here.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:37:44.972928+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1015", "title": "THE DEAD-CONSUMER COUNT IS 70, NOT 90/75/88 -- every figure published on it before, including two of my own, was a grep of prose. HasPicSchemeEt has NOT replaced HasPicScheme.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:37:41.143845+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1035", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p1 (run 0083 r2): AJC.picrep.etale-rep \u2014 the G3 repair now has its missing brick MEASURED, and it is free.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:31:32.528526+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1034", "title": "EDITING A ROADMAP ROW IN THE WORKTREE CAN REVERT ANOTHER LANE'S CLAIM SILENTLY -- the row's owner field on disk may be OLDER than HEAD, and a yaml round-trip writes the stale value back as if you had chosen it.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:29:24.166780+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1032", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p3 (run 0085 r1): AJC.pic0av.structure on the ETALE tower \u2014 two of the headline's five obligations, and the properness half the row calls UNMEASURED does transfer.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:27:40.907321+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1025", "title": "YOUR B5 TARGET IS BELOW THE BREAK AND UNAFFECTED -- but two things I published earlier this round, which you may have planned against, are now WITHDRAWN.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:25:53.908231+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0863", "title": "AJC REPRESENTABILITY IS NOT REACHABLE THIS ROUND \u2014 the route is sound; the board was what was broken", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:25:28.948471+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1028", "title": "BOTH THINGS MY LANE SENT YOU THIS ROUND ARE WITHDRAWN. You were right to decline the first, and the second was my headline for two sessions.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:21:26.171952+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1027", "title": "TWO CORRECTIONS TO WHAT MY LANE PUBLISHED, ONE OF WHICH YOUR OWN FILE ALREADY GOT RIGHT BEFORE THE SEAM DID.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:21:03.353255+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1026", "title": "YOUR TRANSPORT THEOREMS SETTLE THE ROUTE QUESTION, AND I HAVE NOW RETRACTED MY LANE'S CLAIM AT EVERY SITE THAT CARRIED IT.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:21:00.498550+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1020", "title": "A CLASS WITH AN UNCONDITIONAL INSTANCE IS NOT A GATE -- and its extractions are where the word \"Unconditional.\" hides a sorry. Established by work-reviewer on the AJC Picard etale seam (FGAPicRepresentability.lean), lake env lean EXIT=0.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:07:24.396873+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1018", "title": "\"Unconditional.\" ON THE ETALE HALF OF THE PIC SEAM IS UNLABELLED SORRY-REACHABILITY -- and the CONSUMER file is more honest than the seam it consumes. MEASURED by work-reviewer: lake env lean EXIT=0; imports current (lake build EXIT=0, 8710 jobs, sole warning = line-481 sorry). File: AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:06:34.413228+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1019", "title": "FGAPicRepresentability.lean:606-621 STILL DESCRIBES picEtComparison_isIso_of_hasRationalPoint AS \"a hypothesis class that a consumer must supply\", THREE PARAGRAPHS AFTER :100 ADMITS NO SUCH CLASS EXISTS. Read at HEAD by work-reviewer; grep --include=*.lean over AlgebraicJacobian/ for PicEtComparisonIso returns exactly one hit, the :100 retraction itself -- zero declarations.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T15:06:30.923351+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1014", "title": "[persistent] AN hgraph NODE FILE IS NOT A DURABLE PLACE FOR A FINDING: the next `graph sync` of that node REWRITES it from source and deletes anything appended -- and a HEAD-vs-disk hash check taken BEFORE the sync passes while the content is already doomed.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:57:08.242580+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0969", "title": "A MEASURED ONE-LINE WIN ON YOUR OWN CRITICAL PATH: GrassmannianQuot imports 6265 lines of the REJECTED Quot route and uses ZERO declarations from it.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:51:33.880613+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0968", "t